$ cessna210_flagship_trim.bdf — SOL 144 static trim driver (Step 65)
$
$ Thin case-control driver over the shared flagship bulk model.  Two symmetric
$ longitudinal trims of the same airplane at the same flight condition:
$
$   SUBCASE 1  TRIM 1   1g cruise      q = 2334 Pa, V = 61.7 m/s (120 kt)
$   SUBCASE 2  TRIM 2   2.5g pull-up   same q, PITCH = (n-1)*g*c/(2V^2)
$
$ Outputs: .f06 (trim variables, three stability-derivative columns, hinge
$ moments, aero totals, divergence q, displacements, CBAR loads, monitor
$ point integrated loads), <stem>.aero_loads.bdf, <stem>.maneuver_loads.bdf
$ and <stem>.monitor_loads.csv.
$
$ Walk-through: docs/20_theory/02_realistic_airplane_sol144.md
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa, s)
$
SOL 144
TITLE = Cessna 210 flagship — 1g cruise and 2.5g pull-up
INCLUDE 'cessna210_flagship_bulk.bdf'
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = 1g cruise, q = 2334 Pa
  TRIM  = 1
  SPC   = 1
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  FORCE        = ALL
$
SUBCASE 2
  TITLE = 2.5g symmetric pull-up
  TRIM  = 2
  SPC   = 1
  DISPLACEMENT = ALL
  FORCE        = ALL
$
BEGIN BULK
ENDDATA
